  "minutes": 143.5,
  "report": "## Report for m-pv4ger-seg\n\n**Best config (trial t10):** Unet with a resnet34 encoder, `img_size` 320 (native), `dice_weight` 0.3, 25 epochs, default lr. It scored **validation mIoU 0.9590** (foreground IoU 0.9347).\n\n**Confirmation:** I reran the same config with `seed` 1 and got 0.9583 (best epoch 22), a drop of only 0.07 points. That is within noise, so the result holds. The same config with `dice_weight` 1 scored 0.9575 and 0.9576 on two seeds. So the gain from 25 epochs is solid, at about +0.2 points over the 15-epoch baseline of 0.9554. The gain from `dice_weight` 0.3 is marginal, at about +0.1 points and under the noise level.\n\n**What helped**\n- A longer schedule (25 epochs instead of 15) was the main gain. The curves were still rising at epoch 15.\n- A lower `dice_weight` of 0.3 gave a small gain, probably because foreground is about 19% of pixels, so Dice is less important here.\n\n**What did not help** (15-epoch trials score against the 0.9554 baseline)\n\n| Change | Val score |\n|---|---|\n| DeepLabV3Plus (15 epochs) | 0.9522 |\n| DeepLabV3Plus (25 epochs, dice 0.3) | 0.9536 |\n| resnet50 encoder | 0.9535 |\n| resnet18 encoder | 0.9530 |\n| lr 1e-3 | 0.9513 |\n| lr 1e-4 | 0.9541 |\n| `img_size` 416 (upsampling) | 0.9533 |\n\n**Stopping:** I stopped with 3 trials unused. The last 3 trials (t11\u2013t13) did not beat t10, and the stop rule is 3 consecutive non-improving trials.\n\n**What I would try next**\n- Run 40 or more epochs, since the curve was still creeping up at the end.\n- Try Unet++ or an FPN decoder, if the config allows them.\n- Try a stronger pretrained encoder, such as a ResNeXt or EfficientNet variant.\n- Average predictions over test-time flips and rotations.\n\nTreat gaps under about 0.3 points between configs as noise on this 403-image validation set.\n",
